72::
100:
The parameter %.16s\n
does not corresponding to any loaded\n
text file.
101:
Check if the text file is\n
(correct) installed.
102:
There is no valid data object for the\n
inparameter %s of the\n
instruction %s.
103:
Check if there is a right data object.
104:
The SHELL-RAPID user error number\n
%.16s must be declared as a\n
global one.
105:
Check the errnum declaration.
106:
Booking of the new error number\n
%.16s failed. The init value\n
must be -1 or the old no.
107:
Check the init value of the new errnum\n
variable.
